                <pb facs="0750" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.60m/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-04T17:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Lithuania maintaining non committal attitude Polish and Russian efforts to
                    enlist her support and has requested advice of England which has not yet replied
                    but answer expected shortly. Chief of French military mission Kovno leaving
                    to-day for Warsaw to ascertain maximum Polish concession to Lithuania in return
                    for latter’s friendly neutrality.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
